<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<usx version="3.1">
<book code="PHP" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">Philippians</para>

<para style="toc1">Philippians</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="PHP 1"/>

<para style="s">Greetings from Paul and Timothy</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PHP 1:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Philemon 1:1–3</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Colossians 1:1–2</char></note>Paul and Timothy, servants of Christ Jesus,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of Jesus Christ</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; similarly in verse 8</char></note> </para>

<para style="p" vid="PHP 1:1">To all the saints in Christ Jesus being in Philippi, with the overseers and deacons: <verse eid="PHP 1:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PHP 1:2"/>Grace to you⁺ and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ. <verse eid="PHP 1:2"/></para>

<para style="s">Thanksgiving and Prayer1 Corinthians 1:4–9</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PHP 1:3"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Colossians 1:3–14</char></note>I thank my God upon every remembrance of you⁺, <verse eid="PHP 1:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PHP 1:4"/>always in my every supplication for all of you⁺, making the supplication with joy, <verse eid="PHP 1:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PHP 1:5"/>for your⁺ partnership in the gospel from the first day until now, <verse eid="PHP 1:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PHP 1:6"/>being persuaded of this very thing, that the One having begun a good work in you⁺ will complete <char style="add">it</char> until the day of Christ Jesus.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC, F35, TR, and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Jesus Christ</char></note> <verse eid="PHP 1:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PHP 1:7"/>Accordingly, it is right for me to think this about all of you⁺, because of me having you⁺ in the heart. Both in my chains and in the defense and confirmation of the gospel, you⁺ all are fellow partakers of grace with me. <verse eid="PHP 1:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PHP 1:8"/>For God <char style="add">is</char> my witness how I long for you⁺ all in the inner affections of Christ Jesus. <verse eid="PHP 1:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PHP 1:9"/>And this I pray, that your⁺ love may abound yet more and more in knowledge and all discernment, <verse eid="PHP 1:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PHP 1:10"/>for you⁺ to approve the things being excellent, so that you⁺ may be pure and blameless unto the day of Christ, <verse eid="PHP 1:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PHP 1:11"/>being filled with the fruit of righteousness that <char style="add">is</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the fruits of righteousness that are</char></note> through Jesus Christ, to the glory and praise of God. <verse eid="PHP 1:11"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul’s Trials Advance the GospelJames 1:2–12</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PHP 1:12"/>Now I want you⁺ to know brothers, that the things concerning me really have come to the advancement of the gospel, <verse eid="PHP 1:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PHP 1:13"/>so as for my chains in Christ to have become manifest in all the Praetorium<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the whole palace guard</char></note> and to all the rest; <verse eid="PHP 1:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PHP 1:14"/>and most of the brothers, trusting in the Lord by my chains, dare more abundantly to speak fearlessly the word.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> NE and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the word of God</char></note> <verse eid="PHP 1:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PHP 1:15"/>Indeed, some, even through envy and strife, but some also through goodwill, preach Christ— <verse eid="PHP 1:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PHP 1:16"/>the ones indeed out of love, knowing that I am appointed for the defense of the gospel;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR reverse the order of verses 16 and 17.</char></note> <verse eid="PHP 1:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PHP 1:17"/>but the <char style="add">others</char> proclaim Christ out of self-interest, not purely, supposing to add tribulation to my chains. <verse eid="PHP 1:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PHP 1:18"/>What then?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">What then is the issue?</char></note> Only that in every way, whether in pretext or in truth, Christ is proclaimed. And in this I rejoice. Yes, and I will rejoice, <verse eid="PHP 1:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PHP 1:19"/>for I know that this will turn out for me to deliverance, through your⁺ supplication and the supply of the Spirit of Jesus Christ, <verse eid="PHP 1:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PHP 1:20"/>according to my eager expectation and hope that I will be ashamed in nothing, but in all boldness, as always, also now, Christ will be magnified in my body, whether through life or through death. <verse eid="PHP 1:20"/></para>

<para style="s">To Live Is Christ</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PHP 1:21"/>For to me, to live <char style="add">is</char> Christ and to die <char style="add">is</char> gain. <verse eid="PHP 1:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PHP 1:22"/>But if <char style="add">I am</char> to live in flesh, this for me <char style="add">is</char> the fruit of work; and what will I choose? I do not know. <verse eid="PHP 1:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PHP 1:23"/>But<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">For</char></note> I am pressed by the two, having the desire to depart and to be with Christ, for<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for</char></note> <char style="add">it is</char> very much better, <verse eid="PHP 1:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PHP 1:24"/>but to remain in the flesh <char style="add">is</char> more necessary on account of you⁺. <verse eid="PHP 1:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PHP 1:25"/>And having been persuaded of this, I know that I will remain and will continue with all of you⁺ for your⁺ progress and joy of the faith, <verse eid="PHP 1:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PHP 1:26"/>so that through my coming to you⁺ again your⁺ boasting in me may abound in Christ Jesus. <verse eid="PHP 1:26"/></para>

<para style="s">Worthy of the Gospel</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PHP 1:27"/>Only conduct yourselves worthily of the gospel of Christ, so that, whether having come and having seen you⁺, or being absent, I might hear the things concerning you⁺, that you⁺ stand firm in one spirit, contending together with one mind<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">contending side by side</char></note> for the faith of the gospel, <verse eid="PHP 1:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PHP 1:28"/>and not being frightened in <char style="add">anything</char> by those opposing <char style="add">you</char>, which is<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">indeed</char></note> a demonstration of destruction to them, but of salvation to you⁺—and this from God. <verse eid="PHP 1:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PHP 1:29"/>For it was granted to you⁺ on behalf of Christ not only to believe in Him, but also to suffer on behalf of Him, <verse eid="PHP 1:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PHP 1:30"/>having the same struggle such as you⁺ saw in me and now hear of in me. <verse eid="PHP 1:30"/></para>

<chapter eid="PHP 1"/>

<chapter number="2" style="c" sid="PHP 2"/>

<para style="s">One in Christ</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PHP 2:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Ephesians 2:11–18</char></note>Therefore, if <char style="add">there is</char> any encouragement in Christ, if any comfort of love, if any fellowship of the Spirit, if any inner affections and compassions, <verse eid="PHP 2:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PHP 2:2"/>fulfill my joy so that you⁺ may be of the same mind, having the same love, united in soul, minding the one thing, <verse eid="PHP 2:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PHP 2:3"/>nothing according to self-interest or according to vain conceit, but in humility esteeming one another surpassing yourselves, <verse eid="PHP 2:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PHP 2:4"/>each looking at not the things of yourselves, but each also the things of others. <verse eid="PHP 2:4"/></para>

<para style="s">The Mind of ChristIsaiah 52:13–15</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PHP 2:5"/>Let this mind be in you⁺ that <char style="add">was</char> also in Christ Jesus: <verse eid="PHP 2:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PHP 2:6"/>Who, existing in the form of God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PHP 2:6">did not consider to be equal with God </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PHP 2:6">something to be grasped,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">something to be exploited</char></note> <verse eid="PHP 2:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PHP 2:7"/>but emptied Himself, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PHP 2:7">having taken the form of a servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PHP 2:7">having been made in the likeness of men. <verse eid="PHP 2:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PHP 2:8"/>And having been found in appearance as a man </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PHP 2:8">He humbled Himself, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PHP 2:8">having become obedient unto death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PHP 2:8">even the death of the cross. <verse eid="PHP 2:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PHP 2:9"/>Therefore God also highly exalted Him </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PHP 2:9">and granted to Him the name above every name, <verse eid="PHP 2:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PHP 2:10"/>that at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PHP 2:10">in the heavens and on earth and under the earth, <verse eid="PHP 2:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PHP 2:11"/>and every tongue should confess that Jesus Christ <char style="add">is</char> Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PHP 2:11">to the glory of God the Father. <verse eid="PHP 2:11"/></para>

<para style="s">Lights in the WorldMatthew 5:13–16</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PHP 2:12"/>Therefore, my beloved, just as always you⁺ obeyed, not only as in my presence, but now much more in my absence, work out your own salvation with fear and trembling. <verse eid="PHP 2:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PHP 2:13"/>For God is the One working in you⁺ both to will and to work on behalf of <char style="add">His</char> good pleasure. <verse eid="PHP 2:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PHP 2:14"/>Do all things without grumblings and disputings, <verse eid="PHP 2:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PHP 2:15"/>so that you⁺ may be blameless and innocent, children of God unblemished in the midst of a crooked and perverse generation, among whom you⁺ shine as lights in the world, <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Deuteronomy 32:5</char></note><verse eid="PHP 2:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PHP 2:16"/>holding forth the word of life for a boast to me in the day of Christ that I did not run in vain, nor did I toil in vain. <verse eid="PHP 2:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PHP 2:17"/>But even if I am being poured out as a drink offering on the sacrifice and service of your⁺ faith, I rejoice and rejoice with you⁺ all. <verse eid="PHP 2:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PHP 2:18"/>And likewise you⁺ also be glad and rejoice with me. <verse eid="PHP 2:18"/></para>

<para style="s">Timothy and Epaphroditus1 Corinthians 16:10–12</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PHP 2:19"/>But I hope in the Lord Jesus to send Timothy to you⁺ soon, that I also may be of good spirit, having known the things concerning you⁺. <verse eid="PHP 2:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PHP 2:20"/>For I have no one like-minded, who genuinely will care for the things concerning you⁺. <verse eid="PHP 2:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PHP 2:21"/>For those all seek the things of themselves, not the things of Jesus Christ.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> NE, WH, BYZ, and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Christ Jesus</char></note> <verse eid="PHP 2:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PHP 2:22"/>But you⁺ know his proven worth, that as a child <char style="add">with</char> a father he served with me in the gospel. <verse eid="PHP 2:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PHP 2:23"/>Therefore indeed I hope to send him immediately, when I shall have seen the things concerning me. <verse eid="PHP 2:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PHP 2:24"/>And I am persuaded in the Lord that I myself will also come soon. <verse eid="PHP 2:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PHP 2:25"/>Now I deemed <char style="add">it</char> necessary to send to you⁺ Epaphroditus, my brother and fellow worker and fellow soldier, and your⁺ messenger and minister of my need, <verse eid="PHP 2:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PHP 2:26"/>since he was longing for<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">longing to see</char></note> you⁺ all and being deeply distressed because you⁺ heard that he was sick. <verse eid="PHP 2:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PHP 2:27"/>And indeed he was sick, nearly unto death. But God had mercy on him, and not on him only but also on me, that I might not have sorrow upon sorrow. <verse eid="PHP 2:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PHP 2:28"/>Therefore I sent him all the more eagerly, so that having seen him again you⁺ may rejoice, and I may be less anxious. <verse eid="PHP 2:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PHP 2:29"/>Therefore receive him in the Lord with all joy, and hold such in honor, <verse eid="PHP 2:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PHP 2:30"/>because on account of the work of Christ<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the Lord</char></note> he drew near unto death, having disregarded <char style="add">his</char> life so that he might fill up your⁺ deficiency of service toward me. <verse eid="PHP 2:30"/></para>

<chapter eid="PHP 2"/>

<chapter number="3" style="c" sid="PHP 3"/>

<para style="s">Righteousness through Faith in Christ</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PHP 3:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Romans 3:21–31</char></note>Finally, my brothers, rejoice in the Lord. To write the same things to you⁺ indeed <char style="add">is</char> not troublesome to me, and <char style="add">is</char> secure for you⁺. <verse eid="PHP 3:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PHP 3:2"/>Look out for the dogs! Look out for the evil workers! Look out for the mutilation! <verse eid="PHP 3:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PHP 3:3"/>For we are the circumcision, those worshiping in the Spirit of God<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">worshiping God by the Spirit</char></note> and boasting in Christ Jesus, and not having put confidence in the flesh— <verse eid="PHP 3:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PHP 3:4"/>though I have confidence even in the flesh. If any other thinks to have confidence in the flesh, I more: <verse eid="PHP 3:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PHP 3:5"/>circumcision <char style="add">on</char> the eighth day; of the nation of Israel, of the tribe of Benjamin; a Hebrew of Hebrews; according to the law, a Pharisee; <verse eid="PHP 3:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PHP 3:6"/>according to zeal, persecuting the church; according to righteousness that <char style="add">is</char> in the law, having become blameless. <verse eid="PHP 3:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PHP 3:7"/>But whatever things were gain to me, these I have deemed loss because of Christ. <verse eid="PHP 3:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PHP 3:8"/>But indeed, therefore, I also deem all things to be loss because of the surpassing knowledge of Christ Jesus my Lord, because of whom I have lost all things and deem <char style="add">them</char> rubbish, that I may gain Christ <verse eid="PHP 3:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PHP 3:9"/>and may be found in Him, not having my own righteousness that <char style="add">is</char> of the law, but that which <char style="add">is</char> through faith from Christ,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">through the faithfulness of Christ</char></note> the righteousness of God upon faith, <verse eid="PHP 3:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PHP 3:10"/>to know Him and the power of His resurrection and the fellowship of His sufferings, being conformed to His death, <verse eid="PHP 3:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PHP 3:11"/>if somehow I may attain to the resurrection out from the dead. <verse eid="PHP 3:11"/></para>

<para style="s">Pressing on toward the Goal</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PHP 3:12"/>Not that I already obtained <char style="add">it</char> or already have been perfected, but I pursue, if also I may take hold of that for which also I was taken hold of by Christ Jesus.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> SBL </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Christ</char></note> <verse eid="PHP 3:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PHP 3:13"/>Brothers, I do not reckon myself<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC, ALT, F35, and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">reckon myself yet</char></note> to have taken hold <char style="add">of it</char>. But one thing: Indeed, forgetting the things behind and stretching forward to the things ahead, <verse eid="PHP 3:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PHP 3:14"/>I pursue toward the goal for the prize of the upward calling of God in Christ Jesus. <verse eid="PHP 3:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PHP 3:15"/>Therefore as many as <char style="add">are</char> mature, we should be of this mind. And if you⁺ are minded <char style="add">in</char> anything differently, even this God will reveal to you⁺. <verse eid="PHP 3:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PHP 3:16"/>However, to that which we have attained, walk by the same.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">by the same rule, being of the same mind</char></note> <verse eid="PHP 3:16"/></para>

<para style="s">Citizenship in Heaven</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PHP 3:17"/>Be imitators together of me, brothers, and look at those walking thus, as you⁺ have a pattern in us. <verse eid="PHP 3:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PHP 3:18"/>For many walk—<char style="add">of</char> whom I told you⁺ often, and now I say even weeping—<char style="add">as</char> enemies of the cross of Christ, <verse eid="PHP 3:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PHP 3:19"/>whose end <char style="add">is</char> destruction, whose god <char style="add">is</char> the belly and <char style="add">their</char> glory <char style="add">is</char> in their shame, those minding earthly things. <verse eid="PHP 3:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PHP 3:20"/>For our citizenship is in the heavens, from where also we eagerly await a Savior, the Lord Jesus Christ, <verse eid="PHP 3:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PHP 3:21"/>who will transform our body of humiliation <char style="add">to be</char> conformed to the body of His glory, according to the working of His powering, even to subject all things to Himself. <verse eid="PHP 3:21"/></para>

<chapter eid="PHP 3"/>

<chapter number="4" style="c" sid="PHP 4"/>

<para style="s">Rejoice in the Lord</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PHP 4:1"/>Therefore my brothers, beloved and longed for, my joy and crown, in this way stand firm in the Lord, beloved. <verse eid="PHP 4:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PHP 4:2"/>I exhort Euodia and I exhort Syntyche to be of the same mind in the Lord. <verse eid="PHP 4:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PHP 4:3"/>Yes, and<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And also</char></note> I ask you, genuine yokefellow,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I ask you, genuine Syzygus</char></note> assist these <char style="add">women</char> who in the gospel contended together with me, with Clement also and the rest of my fellow workers, whose names <char style="add">are</char> in the book of life. <verse eid="PHP 4:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PHP 4:4"/>Rejoice in the Lord always; again I will say, rejoice! <verse eid="PHP 4:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PHP 4:5"/>Let your⁺ gentleness be known to all men. The Lord <char style="add">is</char> near. <verse eid="PHP 4:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PHP 4:6"/>Be anxious about nothing, but in everything, by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving, let your⁺ requests be made known to God. <verse eid="PHP 4:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PHP 4:7"/>And the peace of God, that is surpassing all understanding, will guard your⁺ hearts and your⁺ minds in Christ Jesus. <verse eid="PHP 4:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PHP 4:8"/>Finally, brothers, whatever is true, whatever <char style="add">is</char> honorable, whatever <char style="add">is</char> right, whatever <char style="add">is</char> pure, whatever <char style="add">is</char> lovely, whatever <char style="add">is</char> well spoken of—if any excellence and if any praise—think on these things. <verse eid="PHP 4:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PHP 4:9"/>And what you⁺ learned and received and heard and saw in me, practice these things. And the God of peace will be with you⁺. <verse eid="PHP 4:9"/></para>

<para style="s">The Generosity of the Philippians2 Corinthians 8:1–15</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PHP 4:10"/>But I rejoiced greatly in the Lord that now at last you⁺ revived <char style="add">your</char> being mindful for me, upon whom also you⁺ were mindful, but you⁺ were lacking opportunity. <verse eid="PHP 4:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PHP 4:11"/>Not that I speak according to deficiency, for I have learned to be content in that which I am. <verse eid="PHP 4:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PHP 4:12"/>I know also <char style="add">how</char> to be brought low, and I know <char style="add">how</char> to abound. In everything and in all things, I have learned the secret also to be full and to hunger, also to abound and to be deficient. <verse eid="PHP 4:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PHP 4:13"/>I have strength <char style="add">for</char> all things in the One empowering me.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the One empowering me—Christ</char></note> <verse eid="PHP 4:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PHP 4:14"/>However, you⁺ did well having fellowship in my affliction. <verse eid="PHP 4:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PHP 4:15"/>And you⁺ also know, Philippians, that in the beginning of the gospel, when I went out from Macedonia, not one church shared with me as to the matter of giving and receiving, except you⁺ only. <verse eid="PHP 4:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PHP 4:16"/>For even in Thessalonica, both once and twice, you⁺ sent for my need. <verse eid="PHP 4:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PHP 4:17"/>Not that I seek after the gift, but I seek after the fruit abounding to your⁺ account. <verse eid="PHP 4:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PHP 4:18"/>But I have all things, and I abound. I have been filled, having received from Epaphroditus the things from you⁺, a fragrance of a sweet smell, an acceptable sacrifice, well-pleasing to God. <verse eid="PHP 4:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PHP 4:19"/>And my God will fill all your⁺ need according to His riches in glory in Christ Jesus. <verse eid="PHP 4:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PHP 4:20"/>Now to our God and Father <char style="add">be</char> the glory to the ages of the ages. Amen. <verse eid="PHP 4:20"/></para>

<para style="s">Final GreetingsEphesians 6:21–24</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PHP 4:21"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Timothy 4:19–22</char></note>Greet every saint in Christ Jesus. </para>

<para style="p" vid="PHP 4:21">The brothers with me greet you⁺. <verse eid="PHP 4:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PHP 4:22"/>All the saints greet you⁺, and especially those of Caesar's household. <verse eid="PHP 4:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PHP 4:23"/>The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ <char style="add">be</char> with your⁺ spirit.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Amen.</char></note> <verse eid="PHP 4:23"/></para>

<chapter eid="PHP 4"/>

</usx>
